[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3167722574","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109411#issuecomment-3167722574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109411","id":3167722574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68z5xO","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-08T12:28:25Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T12:32:59Z","body":"I'm not sure what the issue is here, is it that it fires the signal on load when this particular size is used? This sounds like it's respecting the minimum size given by the standard style, which is the margins of the stylebox (which is probably based on the corner radius, which is 6) and the standard font size (which is 16), and the content margins (which are 2), that *should* add up to 26 or 28. So the minimum height of a standard progress bar is 26 or 28 unsure which\n\nSo it *should* as far as I know adjust its size so it actually follows this limitation, I don't think there's a bug here but actually the proper behavior of the progress bar\n\nIf you want it to behave differently you need to change the standard theme of the progress bar\n\nTo confirm this try calling `get_minimum_size` on the progress bar","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3167722574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3170464037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109411#issuecomment-3170464037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109411","id":3170464037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68-XEl","user":{"login":"Harold12Harvey","id":225528487,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFKpw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225528487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey","html_url":"https://github.com/Harold12Harvey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Harold12Harvey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-09T07:40:48Z","updated_at":"2025-08-09T07:40:48Z","body":"Interesting find! It’s odd that having a progress bar height below 27 would trigger _resized. This might be a side effect of how Godot’s layout system handles minimum sizes. It could be worth experimenting with different threshold values to see if the behavior changes, which might help determine whether it’s a hardcoded limit or something deeper in the layout logic. An MRP would definitely help pinpoint the issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3170464037/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3170474941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109411#issuecomment-3170474941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109411","id":3170474941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68-Zu9","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-09T08:01:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-09T08:01:23Z","body":"It resizes because it figures out its minimum size, I'd say it's desirable to have it tell you it ended up resizing so the size wasn't what you set it to\n\nThere is an MRP though, when I looked at it it was detailed enough to show this behavior ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3170474941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571206134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109411#issuecomment-3571206134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109411","id":3571206134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U3Ef2","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T14:57:11Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T14:57:11Z","body":"I can't seem to reproduce this in 4.5-stable as it wouldn't open with the ANGLE backend. Can someone else reproduce this? My system information: `Godot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL ES 3/A